{
  "name": "l0_entity_parenting",
  "about": "`CBaseEntity::SetParent` 0x100a0670 and its chain (`walks/L0-r010.md`). At map parse (0x10136650) every row's `parentname` is resolved before any Spawn and `SetParent(this, parent, 0)` runs: `kid` and `kid2` hang under `par_a` (yaw 0), so after load `kid.m_pMoveParent == par_a`, `par_a.m_pMoveChild` is the LAST prepended child, `kid.m_pParent == par_a`, `kid.m_iParent == \"par_a\"`, `m_iParentAttachment == 0` (every corpus caller passes 0), the LOCAL words (slots 220/221) are the parent-relative pose (`kid` at +150 +50 +20 cm of `par_a`, angles 0) and the absolute pose (slot 217, which recomputes under EFL 0x800 as 0x100b1ac0 does) is the authored world pose. The `SetParent` input (0x100ad030 -> the by-name overload 0x100a04e0 -> 0x100a0670) reparents `kid` to `par_b` (Unreal yaw 90 = Source yaw -90, 300 200 0): the unlink 0x1012c840 -> 0x1012c6c0 (par_a's chain loses kid) -> 0x1012c7f0 (`SetAngles(GetAbsAngles())`, `SetOrigin(GetAbsOrigin())`), then the prepend 0x1012c7a0, the parent pose 0x101d1530 (AngleMatrix of par_b's absolute pose), the local conversion 0x101d15f0 / 0x100a0a10 / 0x1024da80 / 0x1024cf80 / 0x100a0990 / 0x10137ed0: `o = R^T (c - t)` = (-150, +50, +20) cm in the port's reflected axes and local angles (0, 90, 0); slot 64 and `UTIL_SetOrigin(.., bTouch=0)` 0x101cf5c0 write them (no PhysicsTouchTriggers); the parent's slot 115 is the empty 0x10026bf0. `ClearParent` (0x100ad100 -> 0x1012c840) leaves `m_pParent`, `m_iParent` and `m_iParentAttachment` as they were, clears `m_pMoveParent` / `m_pMovePeer` and par_b's `m_pMoveChild`; its `SetAngles(abs)` differs from the local (0, 90, 0), so it SETS EFL 0x800, and the `GetAbsOrigin()` that follows recomputes with no parent: abs := LOCAL origin (-150, 50, 20) -- retail's own detach bug, reproduced (Open 5). `kid2`, never read through slot 217 since load, carries the dirty bit SetParent left into its ClearParent: the same arm takes its stale local (0, 80, 0) as its world origin. A `SetParent` naming nobody prints `has bad parent` (0x105558a8) and changes nothing. Reported as `fail`, a link word, a pose word or a site payload differs from retail's.",
  "stage": "arena",
  "seed": 1,
